# Earlier features with a real random bot (m7 tasks 2.1-2.3). Needs Arpgtest online and random bots on (rebuild-and-test
# runs with bots on). The bot is one of the server's own random bots, grouped with Arpgtest for the test.
# The bot is brought only after the mob is at 30: a bot next to it attacks it on its own, which (rightly) locks its level.

# Northshire's zone cap (max level + 15 = 20) would hold its mobs at 20: lifted for the test, as in 10-world-scaling.
> .arpg config set Arpg.Scale.ZoneCapAbove 100
? ok
> .arpg test bot Arpgtest leave
? ok
> .arpg test setup Arpgtest 30 westfall-sentinelhill
? ok .*\(online\)
~ 6000
> .arpg test setup Arpgtest 30 elwynn-northshire
? ok .*\(online\)
~ 6000
> .arpg scale probe Arpgtest 178359
* scaled=30\b

> .arpg test bot Arpgtest join 20
? ok bot=\S+ level=\d+ real=0\b
> .arpg test bot Arpgtest bring
? ok bot=\S+ brought map=0\b
~ 8000

# 2.3 (m2): an item a bot gets for itself rolls no affixes (bots are not real players).
> .arpg test bot Arpgtest item 1489
? ok bot=\S+ item=1489 affixes=0\b

# 2.1 (m1 "Bots are not disturbed"): the bot fights the mob (level 30); Arpgtest comes back at 60; the mob keeps level 30
# while the fight lasts and scales once it ends (10-world-scaling covers the same rule with a stand-in).
> .arpg scale combat Arpgtest 178359 bot
? ok combat bot spawn=178359 bot=\S+ incombat=1
> .arpg test setup Arpgtest 60 elwynn-northshire
? ok .*\(online\)
~ 6000
> .arpg scale combat Arpgtest 178359 status
? incombat=1 victim_player=\S+ real=0 level=30\b
> .arpg scale probe Arpgtest 178359
? scaled=30\b
> .arpg scale combat Arpgtest 178359 off
? ok combat off
> .arpg scale probe Arpgtest 178359
* scaled=60\b

# 2.2 (m5): Arpgtest + the bot in the Deadmines = a party of 2: 45% health / 55% damage, no solo role factor.
> .arpg config set Arpg.Test.RecordEvents 1
? ok
> .arpg dungeon level Arpgtest 36 0
? ok
> .arpg test events Arpgtest clear
? ok
> .arpg test setup Arpgtest 90 deadmines-inside
? ok .*\(online\)
~ 12000
> .arpg test bot Arpgtest bring
? ok bot=\S+ brought map=36\b
~ 12000
> .arpg dungeon info Arpgtest
*10 dungeon map=36 instance=1 raid=0 players=2\b
> .arpg test events Arpgtest
? instance scale map=36 players=2 boss=0 health=0\.450 damage=0\.550

> .arpg test bot Arpgtest leave
? ok bot left
> .arpg config set Arpg.Scale.ZoneCapAbove 15
? ok
> .arpg test setup Arpgtest 20 elwynn-northshire
? ok .*\(online\)
~ 8000
